/**
 * One ready-made diagram per supported type, offered by the example dropdown of the diagram
 * toolbar. Each source uses project management data so that an author can see what the diagram is
 * good for before replacing it with their own content.
 *
 * `type` is the type {@link module:mermaid/diagram_types~detectDiagramType} reports for `source`;
 * the types without an example here are mermaid's own `info` and `error` diagnostics.
 *
 * Each source keeps to what the OpenProject renderer takes, so the example an author picks renders
 * in the document as well: no `subgraph` or multi edges (`A --> B & C`) in the flowchart, one block
 * per line in `block-beta`, an `id[Text]` for every `kanban` item and no `milestone` task in the
 * `gantt`.
 */
